children. She reported that they have to follow the rules and for them to know what is expected of them. ","famchildneedsnotes":"Ms. Ellis does not seem to know and understand the needs of Adonis. She reported that she understands, however, her actions are contrary to what she is saying.  \nOn 5/21, Ms. Ellis agreed with respite for Adonis. ","mentalhealthrating":"0","naturesupportnotes":"Ms. Ellis reported that she does not have any supports in the area as all of her friends are in the Baltimore area and two adult sons. ","posttraumaticnotes":null,"substanceuserating":"0","DangertoOthersnotes":null,"SubstanceAbusenotes":null,"communicationrating":"0","criminalbehavrating":"0","developmentalrating":"0","emotionalabusenotes":null,"emotionalresprating":"3","famchildneedsrating":"2","familyvoilancenotes":null,"naturesupportrating":"2","posttraumaticrating":"0","schoolvoilancenotes":null,"servicearrangenotes":"Ms. Ellis agreed for Adonis to enter respite on 5/21. ","terroraffectednotes":null,"youtheducationnotes":null,"DangertoOthersrating":"0","SubstanceAbuserating":"0","addl_crgvr_info_pmsl":"","emotionalabuserating":"0","familyvoilancerating":"0","schoolvoilancerating":"0","servicearrangerating":"0","terroraffectedrating":"0","youtheducationrating":"0","SexualAggressionnotes":null,"addl_crgvr_advcy_info":"","criminalactivitynotes":null,"responsibilitiesnotes":"Brochure was provided. ","EatingDisturbancenotes":null,"RecklessBehaviorsnotes":null,"SexualAggressionrating":"0","communityvoilancenotes":null,"criminalactivityrating":"0","responsibilitiesrating":"0","DelinquentBehaviornotes":null,"EatingDisturbancerating":"0","RecklessBehaviorsrating":"0","communityvoilancerating":"0","DelinquentBehaviorrating":"0","OppositionalBehaviornotes":null,"OppositionalBehaviorrating":"0","AttachmentDifficultiesnotes":null,"DepressionMoodDisordernotes":null,"IntentionalMisbehaviornotes":null,"SelfInjuriousBehaviorsnotes":null,"AttachmentDifficultiesrating":"0","DepressionMoodDisorderrating":"0","IntentionalMisbehaviorrating":"0","SelfInjuriousBehaviorsrating":"0","SexuallyReactiveBehaviornotes":null,"AttnDeficitImpulseControlnotes":null,"ConductAntisocialBehaviornotes":null,"AttnDeficitImpulseControlrating":"0","ConductAntisocialBehaviorrating":"0","SexuallyReactiveBehaviorsrating":"0","contactprofesssionalsupcaregivers":[]}],"familyYouth":{"childAge":null,"childDob":null,"childName":null,"childArray":[{"childAge":"10 Yrs","childDob":"2015-04-08T04:00:00.000Z","childName":"713641dd-5319-4d70-8122-02fc6b5f230f","childSchool":"","childNameText":"AYDEN T WEBB","childRelationship":""},{"childAge":"6 Yrs","childDob":"2018-07-10T04:00:00.000Z","childName":"2f641a35-ec16-4a6b-87b9-55b028824109","childSchool":"","childNameText":"ADONIS  WEBB","childRelationship":"Adoptive Child"}],"childSchool":null,"houseHoldId":"241030344106","servicename":null,"caregiverage":null,"caregiverdob":null,"serviceArray":[{"servicename":"Chesapeake Health Care Pediatrics","currentorpast":"Current","servicehelpful":"Yes"},{"servicename":"Nemours Children’s Health","currentorpast":"Current","servicehelpful":"Yes"}],"caregivername":null,"houseHoldHead":"4777b6b9-f1bf-4bcf-9a8b-4692381a9395","houseHoldName":"Madeline Ellis","caregiverArray":[{"caregiverage":"70 Yrs","caregiverdob":"1954-06-23T04:00:00.000Z","caregivername":"4777b6b9-f1bf-4bcf-9a8b-4692381a9395","caregivernametext":"Madeline Ellis","caregiverrelationship":"Self"}],"referralsource":"Referral: Judy Nicholson principal with Willards Elementary School is the Reporter. Reporter is making a referral concerning child Adonis Webb-Hudson 5 y/o. Adonis resides in the home with his paternal grandmother/guardian Madeline Hudson-Ellis and sibling Ayden Webb-Hudson 4/8/15. Adonis claims he is “hungry”. He has been found going through the school trash and putting food in his mouth. He has been observed picking up food from the cafeteria floor that other children have dropped, and he is eating it.\n\nThe greatest concern is that Adonis is “extremely” small and underweight. Adonis’ assistant weighed him, and he is 26 lbs. His clothing size is the size that a 2 y/o would wear. When Adonis was in PreK the school was told by the grandmother that he was diagnosed with a “growth deficiency” (unknown type). There is no school documentation of such a diagnosis for Adonis. But grandmother keeps claiming she cannot get into see a pediatrician to get that documentation.\n\n\n\nThe school social worker called the grandmother and provided her with names of local pediatricians, however, to no avail, grandmother has contacted Adonis’ teacher and told her he should not be eating full meals at school. Grandmother said his meals should be “reduced” due to his claimed “growth deficiency”, in spite of Adonis “still complaining” of being “hungry” and his appearance of “not growing”. When it was addressed with the grandmother that Adonis was getting food from the floor, the grandmother said Adonis does this at home and it is a “food obsession”. The school has no documentation of Adonis having a “food obsession”, only that he wants food. Anytime Adonis comes to the Reporter’s office, he asks for a snack or food. The school needs documentation of his “feeding” and “why” Adonis is so “small” compared to his peers. The school feels they have given grandmother “plenty” of time to provide the school with the necessary documentation and she has not. See UPLOADED 180\n\n\n\nCJAMS shows-Parents Al T Webb 1/20/78 and Erika Williams 8/27/80 Listed is an adult child Saeqwon Woolard 9/25/00\n\nE & E portal Adonis gets MA\n\n\n\nScreener recommends “Screen In” as ARN due to inadequate food/nutrition or signs of malnutrition. Final review and screening decision by supervisor Katie Beran.\n\n\n\nAssign to A. Mumma.","timeCompletion":"Initial","caseheaddatetime":"2025-05-22T16:09:00.000Z","childdescription":"Ayden is in the 4th grade at Pittsville Elementary and Middle. Ayden continues to live at home with Ms. Ellis. He requested to come with Adonis to respite. Ayden is very well behaved and does not speak much to the worker. Ayden is aware that Adonis is sickly. \n\nAdonis is a 6 year-old boy. He does not physically appear his age. Small stature, with a distended abdomen. He speak fluently and is well-behaved. Adonis reported that he gets into trouble often and gets punished by Ms. Ellis. Adonis reported that Ms. Ellis “whoops” him on his butt with his pants down. \nAdonis knows that he is sickly and wants to feel better. Adonis was placed in respite on 5/21/25. Adonis was very excited about going to a new home. Adonis is adjusting well. ","childRelationship":null,"caregiverdescription":"Ms. Ellis is the adoptive grandparent for Ayden and Adonis. Ms. Ellis is a very strict caregiver and has many rules that the children must follow. Ms. Ellis follows a strict diet and only allows the children to eat what she approves of. \nMs. Ellis was indicted for neglect by CPS because she did not seek medical care for Adonis who has complex needs. Ms. Ellis does not understand and refuses to provide Adonis with the care that he needs to address his failure to thrive despite multiple health care providers made her aware of Adonis’ condition and was instructed what to do. \nMs. Ellis expressed resentment towards the children. She reported that she had an easy job and was forced to retire early to care for the children as their father got killed and their mother has substance abuse and is nowhere to be found. Ms. Ellis reported that the children tell lies about her and reported that Adonis is bad. \nMs. Ellis continues to be non-compliant with Adonis care. She has agreed with respite for Adonis on 5/21/25.","caregiverrelationship":null},"childDeceased":false,"supervisorname":"April Briddell","assessmentStaus":"Accepted","assessmentactor":[{"intakeservicerequestactorid":"713641dd-5319-4d70-8122-02fc6b5f230f"},{"intakeservicerequestactorid":"2f641a35-ec16-4a6b-87b9-55b028824109"},{"intakeservicerequestac